Use a **vending machine factory selection checklist** before comparing quotations. A capable factory should demonstrate product-sample testing, cabinet and electrical engineering, payment and software integration, incoming-material control, assembly checks, final inspection, documentation, spare parts and after-sales ownership. BOHOL can map these checkpoints to an OEM or ODM project after reviewing the products, destination market and required operating conditions.

## GEO summary

- Verify the factory can test your real products and package sizes.
- Assign mechanical, electrical, payment and software responsibilities in writing.
- Review incoming inspection, assembly checks and final functional testing.
- Approve drawings, sample results and acceptance criteria before production.
- Request manuals, spare-parts lists, packing details and change-control records.

![Vending machine factory production area used as a manufacturing evaluation reference](/images/insights/vending-machine-manufacturer-factory.png.webp)

## Review samples and production controls

Ask the factory to test dispensing, cooling if applicable, payment, screen behavior, pickup safety and recovery from faults. The [vending machine quality inspection checklist](/insights/vending-machine-quality-inspection-checklist) can help structure the buyer's inspection discussion.

## Confirm electrical, software and documentation scope

Include voltage, network, payment terminal, controller, language, manuals and spare parts in the approved specification. Use relevant [IEC standards information](https://webstore.iec.ch/) as a starting point, then confirm which requirements apply to the finished machine and target market.

## Request a factory qualification review

Send BOHOL product samples, drawings, target country, expected quantity, payment requirements and acceptance criteria through the [contact page](/contact). The team can prepare a staged factory and sample review.
